<!--Workspace Documentation — Introduction
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.docgen.workspace.documentation.Introduction-->
<wsdocumentation:Introduction xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:docgen="org.blockml.bml.docgen"
  xmlns:wsdocumentation="org.blockml.bml.docgen.workspace.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Purpose and scope of the BlockML Docgen workspace library
  </is>
  <documentation>
    This repository is the BlockML Docgen monorepo. It authors two @blockml/* packages
    whose BML libraries are the product.
    
    @blockml/docgen is the base library for structuring documentation. It defines how
    human-facing documentation is modelled and manifested from BlockML — DocSet, Page,
    PageGroup, Plans, manifestation stages, page and content types, roles, rules, and
    semantic annotations — without tying those types to one website or programme.
    
    @blockml/bmldocs is a sector model that uses docgen as that structural foundation
    and generates the BlockML documentation in successive steps. Numbered sectors
    (a01, a02, …) each contain an autonomous sub-model; a later sector can be produced
    from an earlier one. Sector models are not classical cohesive libraries.
    
    This workspace library (org.blockml.bml.docgen.workspace.*) is the monorepo
    documentation hub and SSOT entry for humans and LLMs. It links the base package
    library via Library.dependencies (workspace → packages only). Per-package
    contracts stay in those libraries; this hub does not re-export their blocks.
    
    Root README.md points here.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="wsdocumentation:PackageMap" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="wsdocumentation:ArchitectureOverview" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="wsdocumentation:LinkingRules" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="docgen:Library" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</wsdocumentation:Introduction>
